  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b55d6dca",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Convert Class_dates strings into `datetime` format and save the list into variable a"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 25,
   "id": "51582b40",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "[datetime.datetime(2017, 8, 25, 0, 0),\n",
       " datetime.datetime(2017, 9, 1, 0, 0),\n",
       " datetime.datetime(2017, 9, 8, 0, 0),\n",
       " datetime.datetime(2017, 9, 15, 0, 0),\n",
       " datetime.datetime(2017, 9, 22, 0, 0),\n",
       " datetime.datetime(2017, 9, 29, 0, 0)]"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 107,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "[datetime.strptime(x, '%m/%d/%Y') for x in class_dates]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "53128ac2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Use parse() to attempt to auto-convert common string formats. Parser must be a string or character stream, not list."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 26,
   "id": "8b259d54",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 24, 0, 0)"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 108,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "parse(fall_start) "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e85e82e2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Use parse() on every element of the Class_dates string."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 27,
   "id": "02c568f4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "[datetime.datetime(2017, 8, 25, 0, 0),\n",
       " datetime.datetime(2017, 9, 1, 0, 0),\n",
       " datetime.datetime(2017, 9, 8, 0, 0),\n",
       " datetime.datetime(2017, 9, 15, 0, 0),\n",
       " datetime.datetime(2017, 9, 22, 0, 0),\n",
       " datetime.datetime(2017, 9, 29, 0, 0)]"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 109,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "[parse(x) for x in class_dates]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ed27c5fa",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Use parse, but designate that the day is first."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 28,
   "id": "836f860a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 24, 0, 0)"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 110,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "parse (fall_start, dayfirst=True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2a20c958",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Create a `dataframe`. A DataFrame is a tabular data structure comprised of rows and columns, akin to a spreadsheet, database table. DataFrame is a group of Series objects that share an index (the column names)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 29,
   "id": "3008f106",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "                       dates  complete\n",
      "0  8/25/2017 18:47:05.069722         1\n",
      "1   9/1/2017 18:47:05.119994         0\n",
      "2   9/8/2017 18:47:05.178768         1\n",
      "3  9/15/2017 18:47:05.230071         1\n",
      "4  9/22/2017 18:47:05.230071         0\n",
      "5  9/29/2017 18:47:05.280592         1\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "data = {\n",
    "  'dates': [\n",
    "    '8/25/2017 18:47:05.069722',\n",
    "    '9/1/2017 18:47:05.119994',\n",
    "    '9/8/2017 18:47:05.178768',\n",
    "    '9/15/2017 18:47:05.230071',\n",
    "    '9/22/2017 18:47:05.230071',\n",
    "    '9/29/2017 18:47:05.280592'],\n",
    "  'complete': [1, 0, 1, 1, 0, 1]}\n",
    "df = pd.DataFrame(\n",
    "  data,\n",
    "  columns = ['dates','complete'])\n",
    "print(df)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "66f73b6e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Convert `` df[`date`] `` from string to datetime"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 30,
   "id": "1f2331b3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "0   2017-08-25 18:47:05.069722\n",
       "1   2017-09-01 18:47:05.119994\n",
       "2   2017-09-08 18:47:05.178768\n",
       "3   2017-09-15 18:47:05.230071\n",
       "4   2017-09-22 18:47:05.230071\n",
       "5   2017-09-29 18:47:05.280592\n",
       "Name: dates, dtype: datetime64[ns]"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 112,
     "metadata": {},
